---
import Section from '../../../components/ui/Section.astro';
---

<Section class="experience" id="experience" labelledBy="experience-title">
  <div class="section-topline"><span class="index">02 / EXPERIENCE</span><span class="label">Internships</span></div>
  <div class="experience-heading">
    <h2 id="experience-title">Experience<span>.</span></h2>
    <p>My work in product and software engineering, from investigating customer issues to building practical tools.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="experience-list">
    <article class="experience-entry">
      <div class="experience-entry__meta"><span>01 / PRODUCT ENGINEERING</span><span>JUN 2026 — AUG 2026</span></div>
      <div class="experience-entry__body">
        <div><h3>Fin from<br />Salesforce<span class="experience-dot">.</span></h3><p class="experience-role">Product Engineering Intern</p></div>
        <div class="experience-copy"><p>Investigated and resolved customer-impacting issues in Fin Messenger across the web, Android and iOS, reproducing bugs, analysing logs and tracing problems through a production codebase.</p><p>Designed and implemented configurable expiry for Special Notices, allowing notices in the Messenger widget to turn off automatically. I worked with Ruby, TypeScript, JavaScript and AWS.</p><div class="experience-keywords"><span>Ruby</span><span>TypeScript</span><span>JavaScript</span><span>Ember.js</span><span>AWS</span></div></div>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="experience-entry">
      <div class="experience-entry__meta"><span>02 / SOFTWARE ENGINEERING</span><span>JUN 2025 — DEC 2025</span></div>
      <div class="experience-entry__body">
        <div><h3>Cloudcards<span class="experience-dot">.</span></h3><p class="experience-role">Software Engineering Intern</p></div>
        <div class="experience-copy"><p>Designed and built a production desktop application for uploading large aviation datasets, replacing a slower browser-based workflow. It supports chunked, parallel and resumable uploads, with progress tracking and per-file status.</p><p>Worked directly with the operations team from requirements through deployment, using C#, .NET, Blazor Hybrid and WPF, with supporting upload infrastructure on Azure.</p><div class="experience-keywords"><span>C#</span><span>.NET</span><span>WPF</span><span>Blazor Hybrid</span><span>Azure</span></div></div>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div></Section>
